Rem ==================================================================
Rem geo.shoddy — test program for machines/geo.shoddy
Rem
Rem Assert-driven, in the fin.shoddy / eng.shoddy / bool.shoddy pattern:
Rem it prints what it is doing, stops at the first failed assertion, and
Rem ends with ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED when none fail. Offline — nothing
Rem here touches a file, a socket or a window, and nothing here reads a
Rem clock.
Rem
Rem EVERY NUMBER BELOW IS A KNOWN ANSWER, NEVER A VALUE RECORDED FROM A
Rem RUN. The distances and bearings were worked independently, by the
Rem SPHERICAL LAW OF COSINES, before machines/geo.shoddy existed:
Rem
Rem   d = R * acos(sin(lat1) sin(lat2) + cos(lat1) cos(lat2) cos(dLon))
Rem
Rem That matters more here than in most suites. geo computes distance by
Rem HAVERSINE, which is a different formula reaching the same number, so
Rem a fixture worked this way disagrees with a mistyped haversine instead
Rem of agreeing with it. A suite built from geo's own output would agree
Rem with a wrong geo forever.
Rem
Rem   London  51.5074 N, 0.1278 W        Paris     48.8566 N, 2.3522 E
Rem   New York 40.7128 N, 74.0060 W
Rem
Rem   London -> Paris     343556.5349 m   initial 148.1156169 deg
Rem                                       final   150.0210929 deg
Rem   London -> New York 5570229.874  m   initial 288.3297016 deg
Rem                                       final   231.2126168 deg
Rem   0N 179E -> 0N 179W  222390.1605 m
Rem
Rem The wider tolerances in the ACCEPTANCE block are deliberately looser
Rem than the arithmetic needs: what they pin is the formula, not the
Rem coordinates somebody chose for the fixture.
Rem
Rem NOTHING IS ASSERTED WITH = ON A COMPUTED POINT. A GeoPt is an
Rem all-scalar record, so it does compare structurally — but a point
Rem arrived at through trigonometry never lands on the literal it should
Rem equal. GeoNear is the comparison throughout, exactly as EngCNear is
Rem for complex numbers. = appears only on points that were BUILT rather
Rem than computed, where it is testing the constructor and nothing else.
Rem
Rem INCLUDES DO NOT BLEED THROUGH, so math's Rad, Deg and Clamp are not
Rem in scope here even though geo is built on them. Everything below is
Rem a builtin or a Geo word, which is the right constraint for a suite:
Rem it can only reach what a caller of geo can reach.
Rem
Rem WHAT CANNOT BE TESTED HERE: the aborting half of the domain guard.
Rem Shoddy has no catchable errors, so asserting that GeoAt(91, 0)
Rem aborts would kill the suite rather than fail an assertion. The
Rem aborting twin is verified by hand and named here instead:
Rem
Rem   GeoAt(91, 0)        latitude above 90
Rem   GeoAt(-91, 0)       latitude below -90
Rem   GeoAt(0, 181)       longitude outside -180..180
Rem
Rem GeoTryAt is the total twin of exactly those refusals and IS asserted
Rem below, on both arms. That is the argument for the Result/abort line
Rem being drawn where it is.
Rem
Rem Run: bin\mill run tst\geo.shoddy      (from the repo root)
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../machines/geo.shoddy"

Rem ---- fixtures --------------------------------------------------------

Def London() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(51.5074, -0.1278)

Def Paris() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(48.8566, 2.3522)

Def NewYork() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(40.7128, -74.006)

Rem The two points either side of the antimeridian, ON THE EQUATOR. The
Rem latitude has to be stated: the same two degrees of longitude shrink
Rem with the cosine, so a test omitting it asserts an accident.
Def EastOfLine() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(0, 179)

Def WestOfLine() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(0, -179)

Rem The cross-track trio. TrackA -> TrackB runs east-south-east; OffTrack
Rem lies NORTH of it, which is to the LEFT of that heading, which is why
Rem the expected cross-track distance below is negative.
Def TrackA() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(53.3206, -1.7297)

Def TrackB() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(53.1887, -0.1334)

Def OffTrack() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(53.2611, -0.7972)

Rem The intersection worked example: two aircraft on two bearings.
Def IntA() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(51.8853, 0.2545)

Def IntB() As GeoPt
    GeoAt(49.0034, 2.5735)

Rem A three-point route across northern Europe: London, Paris, Lyon.
Def Route() As List Of GeoPt
    { London(), Paris(), GeoAt(45.764, 4.8357) }

Rem The two-point route across the antimeridian, which is where every
Rem bounding box written by hand goes wrong.
Def LineRoute() As List Of GeoPt
    { EastOfLine(), WestOfLine() }

Rem ---- this file's own helpers -----------------------------------------

Def Close(a As Number, b As Number, tol As Number) As Boolean
    Abs(a - b) <= tol

Def IsNone(o As Option) As Boolean
    Select Case o
        Case None
            True
        Case Else
            False

Rem Option has no accessor words — Select Case is the only way in — so
Rem an assertion about the point inside one goes through this.
Def SomeOr(o As Option, dflt As GeoPt) As GeoPt
    Select Case o
        Case Some(p)
            p
        Case Else
            dflt

Rem The degree and second marks, built from their codes rather than
Rem typed. A literal degree sign in a source file is one bad save away
Rem from mojibake, and verify-docs.js scans this tree for exactly that.
Def DegMark() As String
    Chr(176)

Def SecMark() As String
    Chr(34)

Def OkNum(r As Result, dflt As Number) As Number
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(x)
            x
        Case Else
            dflt

Def OkPt(r As Result) As GeoPt
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(p)
            p
        Case Else
            GeoAt(0, 0)

Def OkBox(r As Result) As GeoBox
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(b)
            b
        Case Else
            GeoBox(0, 0, 0, 0, False)

Def ErrAt(r As Result) As Number
    Select Case r
        Case Err(why, at)
            at
        Case Else
            0

Rem seq's Contains is not in scope here — Includes do not bleed through
Rem — so the two list predicates this file needs are its own, on Fold.
Def HasText(xs As List Of String, v As String) As Boolean
    Fold(xs, False, Fn(a, x) => a Or (x = v))

Def CountOf(xs As List Of String, v As String) As Number
    Fold(xs, 0, Fn(a, x) => a + Ifte(x = v, 1, 0))

Def AllDistinct(xs As List Of String) As Boolean
    Fold(xs, True, Fn(a, x) => a And (CountOf(xs, x) = 1))

Rem Comparing two bearings needs the difference folded, or due north
Rem read off a real calculation — 359.97 degrees — is judged 360 away
Rem from 0 rather than a thirtieth of a degree. Every angular assertion
Rem below goes through this and none of them uses Close.
Def CloseAngle(a As Number, b As Number, tol As Number) As Boolean
    Abs(180 - Wrap(180 - (a - b), 360)) <= tol

Def SomeNum(o As Option, dflt As Number) As Number
    Select Case o
        Case Some(x)
            x
        Case Else
            dflt

Def SomeNums(o As Option) As List Of Number
    Select Case o
        Case Some(xs)
            xs
        Case Else
            { }

Def IsErr(r As Result) As Boolean
    Select Case r
        Case Err(why, at)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Rem The round trip that catches everything: steer the bearing geo
Rem answers for the distance geo answers, and arrive back at b.
Def RoundTrips(a As GeoPt, b As GeoPt) As Boolean
    GeoNear(GeoDestination(a, GeoBearing(a, b), GeoDistance(a, b)), b, 1)

Def Main()
    Print("--- THE SPHERE ---")
    Assert(GeoRadius() = 6371008.8, "THE IUGG MEAN EARTH RADIUS, IN METRES")

    Print("--- THE TYPE AND ITS CONSTRUCTION ---")
    Assert(GeoLat(GeoAt(53.72, -1.86)) = 53.72, "LATITUDE IS THE FIRST FIELD")
    Assert(GeoLon(GeoAt(53.72, -1.86)) = -1.86, "AND LONGITUDE THE SECOND")
    Assert(GeoAt(90, 180) = GeoPt(90, 180), "THE CORNERS OF THE DOMAIN ARE INSIDE IT")
    Assert(GeoAt(-90, -180) = GeoPt(-90, -180), "AT BOTH ENDS")

    Print("--- THE DOMAIN, AS A RESULT ---")
    Assert(GeoTryAt(53.72, -1.86) = Ok(GeoPt(53.72, -1.86)), "A GOOD COORDINATE IS OK")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoTryAt(91, 0)), "91 DEGREES NORTH IS ERR, NOT AN ABORT")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoTryAt(-91, 0)), "AND 91 DEGREES SOUTH")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoTryAt(0, 181)), "AND 181 DEGREES EAST")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoTryAt(0, -181)), "AND 181 DEGREES WEST")
    Assert(Not IsErr(GeoTryAt(90, 180)), "THE CORNERS ARE NOT REFUSED")

    Print("--- THE ANTIMERIDIAN, FOLDED ONCE AND FOR ALL ---")
    Assert(GeoWrapLon(0) = 0, "ZERO IS ZERO")
    Assert(GeoWrapLon(179) = 179, "AND ANYTHING ALREADY INSIDE IS UNTOUCHED")
    Assert(GeoWrapLon(180) = 180, "THE RANGE IS HALF-OPEN AT THE WEST END, SO 180 STAYS 180")
    Assert(GeoWrapLon(-180) = 180, "AND -180 IS THE SAME MERIDIAN, SPELLED THE OTHER WAY")
    Assert(GeoWrapLon(190) = -170, "190 EAST IS 170 WEST")
    Assert(GeoWrapLon(-190) = 170, "AND 190 WEST IS 170 EAST")
    Assert(GeoWrapLon(360) = 0, "A WHOLE TURN COMES BACK")
    Assert(GeoWrapLon(540) = 180, "AND A TURN AND A HALF LANDS ON THE LINE")

    Print("--- BEARINGS ARE 0..360, NORTH IS 0, CLOCKWISE ---")
    Assert(GeoWrapBrg(0) = 0, "NORTH IS ZERO")
    Assert(GeoWrapBrg(-170) = 190, "AND NO CALLER EVER SEES -170")
    Assert(GeoWrapBrg(370) = 10, "A TURN AND TEN IS TEN")
    Assert(GeoWrapBrg(360) = 0, "AND A WHOLE TURN IS NORTH AGAIN, NOT 360")

    Print("--- DISTANCE, AGAINST INDEPENDENTLY WORKED VALUES ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), Paris()), 343556.5349, 1), "LONDON TO PARIS, TO THE METRE")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), NewYork()), 5570229.874, 1), "LONDON TO NEW YORK, TO THE METRE")
    Assert(GeoDistance(London(), Paris()) = GeoDistance(Paris(), London()), "DISTANCE IS SYMMETRIC")
    Assert(GeoDistance(London(), London()) = 0, "AND A POINT IS NO DISTANCE FROM ITSELF")

    Print("--- ACCEPTANCE: THE PUBLISHED FIGURES, LOOSELY PINNED ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), Paris()), 344000, 2000), "LONDON TO PARIS IS 344 KM WITHIN 2 KM")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), NewYork()), 5570000, 20000), "LONDON TO NEW YORK IS 5570 KM WITHIN 20 KM")

    Print("--- THE ANTIMERIDIAN IS 222 KM, NOT 40000 ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(EastOfLine(), WestOfLine()), 222390.1605, 1), "179 EAST TO 179 WEST ON THE EQUATOR")
    Assert(GeoDistance(EastOfLine(), WestOfLine()) < 300000, "THE SHORT WAY ROUND, WHICH IS THE WHOLE POINT")

    Print("--- BEARING ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoBearing(London(), Paris()), 148.1156169, 0.0001), "LONDON TO PARIS, INITIAL")
    Assert(Close(GeoBearing(London(), NewYork()), 288.3297016, 0.0001), "LONDON TO NEW YORK, INITIAL")
    Assert(GeoBearing(London(), Paris()) >= 0, "A BEARING IS NEVER NEGATIVE")
    Assert(GeoBearing(London(), NewYork()) < 360, "AND NEVER A WHOLE TURN")

    Print("--- FINAL BEARING IS NOT THE INITIAL ONE REVERSED ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoFinalBearing(London(), Paris()), 150.0210929, 0.0001), "LONDON TO PARIS, ON ARRIVAL")
    Assert(Close(GeoFinalBearing(London(), NewYork()), 231.2126168, 0.0001), "LONDON TO NEW YORK, ON ARRIVAL")
    Assert(Abs(GeoFinalBearing(London(), NewYork()) - GeoWrapBrg(GeoBearing(London(), NewYork()) + 180)) > 50, "AND OVER THE ATLANTIC THE TWO DIFFER BY MORE THAN 50 DEGREES")

    Print("--- THE ROUND TRIP: DESTINATION OVER BEARING OVER DISTANCE ---")
    Assert(RoundTrips(London(), Paris()), "A SHORT LEG RETURNS WITHIN A METRE")
    Assert(RoundTrips(London(), NewYork()), "A LONG ONE DOES TOO")
    Assert(RoundTrips(EastOfLine(), WestOfLine()), "AND ONE CROSSING THE ANTIMERIDIAN")
    Assert(RoundTrips(GeoAt(-33.8688, 151.2093), GeoAt(-41.2865, 174.7762)), "AND ONE IN THE SOUTHERN HEMISPHERE")

    Print("--- DESTINATION ---")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoDestination(London(), 90, 0), London(), 0.000001), "GOING NOWHERE ARRIVES WHERE YOU STARTED")
    Assert(Close(GeoLat(GeoDestination(GeoAt(0, 0), 0, GeoRadius() * Pi() / 2)), 90, 0.000001), "DUE NORTH A QUARTER OF THE WAY ROUND REACHES THE POLE")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), GeoDestination(London(), 37, 100000)), 100000, 0.000001), "AND THE DISTANCE STEERED IS THE DISTANCE TRAVELLED")
    Assert(GeoLon(GeoDestination(EastOfLine(), 90, 400000)) < 0, "STEERING EAST OFF 179 EAST LANDS IN THE WESTERN HEMISPHERE")

    Print("--- MIDPOINT IS NOT THE AVERAGE OF TWO COORDINATES ---")
    Assert(Close(Abs(GeoLon(GeoMidpoint(EastOfLine(), WestOfLine()))), 180, 0.000001), "THE MIDPOINT ACROSS THE LINE IS ON THE LINE")
    Assert(Close(GeoLat(GeoMidpoint(EastOfLine(), WestOfLine())), 0, 0.000001), "AND STAYS ON THE EQUATOR")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), GeoMidpoint(London(), NewYork())), GeoDistance(GeoMidpoint(London(), NewYork()), NewYork()), 0.001), "THE MIDPOINT IS EQUIDISTANT FROM BOTH ENDS")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoMidpoint(London(), London()), London(), 0.000001), "AND THE MIDPOINT OF ONE POINT IS THAT POINT")

    Print("--- ALONG, WHICH MIDPOINT IS HALF OF ---")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoAlong(London(), NewYork(), 0), London(), 0.001), "FRACTION 0 IS THE START")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoAlong(London(), NewYork(), 1), NewYork(), 0.001), "FRACTION 1 IS THE END")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoAlong(London(), NewYork(), 0.5), GeoMidpoint(London(), NewYork()), 0.001), "AND A HALF IS THE MIDPOINT")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), GeoAlong(London(), NewYork(), 0.25)), GeoDistance(London(), NewYork()) * 0.25, 0.001), "A QUARTER OF THE WAY IS A QUARTER OF THE DISTANCE")
    Assert(GeoDistance(London(), GeoAlong(London(), NewYork(), 2)) > GeoDistance(London(), NewYork()), "AND A FRACTION PAST 1 EXTRAPOLATES, DELIBERATELY")

    Print("--- ANTIPODE ---")
    Assert(GeoAntipode(GeoAt(53.72, -1.86)) = GeoPt(-53.72, 178.14), "DIAMETRICALLY OPPOSITE, BOTH FIELDS TURNED")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), GeoAntipode(London())), GeoRadius() * Pi(), 0.001), "AND HALF THE PLANET AWAY")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoAntipode(GeoAntipode(London())), London(), 0.000001), "TWICE OVER IS BACK HOME")

    Print("--- THE POLES ARE THE OTHER BUG ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(GeoAt(90, 0), GeoAt(0, 0)), GeoRadius() * Pi() / 2, 0.001), "POLE TO EQUATOR IS A QUARTER OF THE WAY ROUND")
    Assert(GeoBearing(GeoAt(90, 0), GeoAt(50, 0)) = 180, "EVERY DIRECTION FROM THE NORTH POLE IS SOUTH")
    Assert(GeoBearing(GeoAt(-90, 0), GeoAt(-50, 0)) = 0, "AND EVERY DIRECTION FROM THE SOUTH POLE IS NORTH")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(GeoAt(90, 0), GeoAt(90, 137)), 0, 0.000001), "THE POLE IS ONE PLACE, WHATEVER LONGITUDE IT IS SPELLED WITH")

    Print("--- NEAR, THE ONLY COMPARISON OFFERED ---")
    Assert(GeoNear(London(), London(), 0), "A POINT IS WITHIN NOTHING OF ITSELF")
    Assert(GeoNear(London(), Paris(), 400000), "LONDON IS WITHIN 400 KM OF PARIS")
    Assert(Not GeoNear(London(), Paris(), 1000), "AND NOT WITHIN 1 KM")

    Print("--- EQUIRECTANGULAR, HONEST ABOUT BEING WRONG ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoEquirect(London(), Paris()), GeoDistance(London(), Paris()), 500), "IT IS GOOD ENOUGH TO RANK A SHORTLIST")
    Assert(Abs(GeoEquirect(London(), NewYork()) - GeoDistance(London(), NewYork())) > 100000, "AND OVER THE ATLANTIC IT IS OUT BY OVER 100 KM, WHICH IS WHY IT IS NOT A DISTANCE")
    Assert(GeoEquirect(London(), London()) = 0, "A POINT IS STILL NO DISTANCE FROM ITSELF")

    Print("--- CROSS-TRACK, SIGNED ON PURPOSE ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoCrossTrack(OffTrack(), TrackA(), TrackB()), -1636.588912, 0.01), "THE PERPENDICULAR DISTANCE FROM THE GREAT CIRCLE")
    Assert(GeoCrossTrack(GeoAt(0.4, 0.6), GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(1, 1)) > 0, "RIGHT OF A NORTH-EAST TRACK IS POSITIVE")
    Assert(GeoCrossTrack(GeoAt(0.6, 0.4), GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(1, 1)) < 0, "AND LEFT OF IT IS NEGATIVE")
    Assert(Close(GeoCrossTrack(TrackA(), TrackA(), TrackB()), 0, 0.000001), "A POINT ON THE TRACK IS NOT OFF IT")

    Print("--- ALONG-TRACK ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoAlongTrack(OffTrack(), TrackA(), TrackB()), 62310.85005, 0.01), "HOW FAR ALONG THE NEAREST POINT LIES")
    Assert(Close(GeoAlongTrack(TrackA(), TrackA(), TrackB()), 0, 0.000001), "THE START IS NO WAY ALONG")
    Assert(Close(GeoAlongTrack(TrackB(), TrackA(), TrackB()), GeoDistance(TrackA(), TrackB()), 0.001), "AND THE END IS THE WHOLE WAY")
    Assert(GeoAlongTrack(GeoDestination(TrackA(), GeoWrapBrg(GeoBearing(TrackA(), TrackB()) + 180), 5000), TrackA(), TrackB()) < 0, "A POINT BEHIND THE START IS A NEGATIVE DISTANCE ALONG")

    Print("--- THE FOOT OF THE PERPENDICULAR, CLAMPED TO THE SEGMENT ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(OffTrack(), GeoClosestOnLeg(OffTrack(), TrackA(), TrackB())), 1636.588912, 0.1), "THE NEAREST POINT IS THE CROSS-TRACK DISTANCE AWAY")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoClosestOnLeg(GeoDestination(TrackB(), GeoBearing(TrackA(), TrackB()), 50000), TrackA(), TrackB()), TrackB(), 0.001), "PAST THE END CLAMPS TO THE END")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoClosestOnLeg(GeoDestination(TrackA(), GeoWrapBrg(GeoBearing(TrackA(), TrackB()) + 180), 50000), TrackA(), TrackB()), TrackA(), 0.001), "AND BEFORE THE START CLAMPS TO THE START")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoClosestOnLeg(OffTrack(), TrackA(), TrackA()), TrackA(), 0.000001), "A LEG OF NO LENGTH IS ITS OWN NEAREST POINT")

    Print("--- WHERE TWO GREAT CIRCLES CROSS ---")
    Assert(Not IsNone(GeoIntersect(IntA(), 108.547, IntB(), 32.435)), "TWO CROSSING PATHS CROSS")
    Assert(GeoNear(SomeOr(GeoIntersect(IntA(), 108.547, IntB(), 32.435), GeoAt(0, 0)), GeoPt(50.9078087, 4.508409907), 1), "AND THEY CROSS WHERE THE WORKED EXAMPLE SAYS, WITHIN A METRE")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoIntersect(GeoAt(0, 0), 90, GeoAt(0, 10), 90)), "TWO PATHS ALONG THE EQUATOR ARE ONE CIRCLE, AND ONE CIRCLE HAS NO CROSSING")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoIntersect(GeoAt(0, 0), 90, GeoAt(0, 10), 270)), "AND THE SAME CIRCLE RUN BACKWARDS IS STILL ONE CIRCLE")
    Assert(GeoNear(SomeOr(GeoIntersect(London(), 0, London(), 90), GeoAt(0, 0)), London(), 0.000001), "TWO PATHS FROM ONE POINT CROSS AT THAT POINT")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoIntersect(London(), 45, London(), 225)), "UNLESS THE TWO BEARINGS DESCRIBE ONE CIRCLE")

    Print("--- A ROUTE IS A LIST, AND AN EMPTY ONE HAS A LENGTH ---")
    Assert(GeoRouteLength({ }) = 0, "A ROUTE WITH NOWHERE TO GO IS ZERO LONG, NOT AN ERROR")
    Assert(GeoRouteLength({ London() }) = 0, "AND SO IS A ROUTE OF ONE POINT")
    Assert(Close(GeoRouteLength({ London(), Paris() }), GeoDistance(London(), Paris()), 0.000001), "A TWO-POINT ROUTE IS ONE LEG")
    Assert(Length(GeoRouteLegs(Route())) = 2, "THREE POINTS MAKE TWO LEGS")
    Assert(Length(GeoRouteLegs({ })) = 0, "AND NO POINTS MAKE NO LEGS")
    Assert(Close(Nth(GeoRouteLegs(Route()), 1), GeoDistance(London(), Paris()), 0.000001), "AND THE FIRST LEG IS THE FIRST LEG")

    Print("--- CUMULATIVE: N VALUES, FIRST 0, LAST THE TOTAL ---")
    Assert(Length(GeoRouteCumulative(Route())) = 3, "ONE PER POINT, NOT ONE PER LEG")
    Assert(First(GeoRouteCumulative(Route())) = 0, "THE START IS NO WAY ALONG")
    Assert(Close(Nth(GeoRouteCumulative(Route()), 3), GeoRouteLength(Route()), 0.000001), "AND THE END IS THE WHOLE LENGTH")

    Print("--- THE COURSE TO STEER, LEG BY LEG ---")
    Assert(Length(GeoRouteBearings(Route())) = 2, "ONE BEARING PER LEG")
    Assert(Close(First(GeoRouteBearings(Route())), GeoBearing(London(), Paris()), 0.000001), "AND IT IS THE INITIAL BEARING OF THAT LEG")

    Print("--- THE POINT THAT FAR ALONG, OR ABSENCE ---")
    Assert(GeoNear(SomeOr(GeoRouteAt(Route(), 0), GeoAt(0, 0)), London(), 0.001), "NOTHING ALONG IS THE START")
    Assert(GeoNear(SomeOr(GeoRouteAt(Route(), GeoRouteLength(Route())), GeoAt(0, 0)), Nth(Route(), 3), 0.001), "THE WHOLE WAY ALONG IS THE END")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoRouteAt(Route(), GeoRouteLength(Route()) + 1)), "PAST THE END IS ABSENCE, NOT A CALLER BUG")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoRouteAt(Route(), -1)), "AND SO IS BEFORE THE START")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoRouteAt({ }, 0)), "AN EMPTY ROUTE HAS NO POINT ANYWHERE ALONG IT")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), SomeOr(GeoRouteAt(Route(), 100000), GeoAt(0, 0))), 100000, 0.001), "AND 100 KM ALONG IS 100 KM FROM THE START")

    Print("--- THE NEAREST POINT ON A ROUTE ---")
    Assert(Close(HitAway(GeoNearestOn({ TrackA(), TrackB() }, OffTrack())), 1636.588912, 0.1), "AS FAR OFF AS THE CROSS-TRACK DISTANCE SAYS")
    Assert(HitLeg(GeoNearestOn({ TrackA(), TrackB() }, OffTrack())) = 1, "ON THE FIRST LEG")
    Assert(Close(HitAlong(GeoNearestOn({ TrackA(), TrackB() }, OffTrack())), 62310.85005, 0.5), "AND THAT FAR ALONG IT")
    Assert(HitLeg(GeoNearestOn(Route(), GeoAt(46, 5))) = 2, "A POINT BY LYON IS NEAREST THE SECOND LEG")
    Assert(GeoNear(HitPoint(GeoNearestOn({ London() }, Paris())), London(), 0.000001), "A ONE-POINT ROUTE IS ITS OWN NEAREST POINT")

    Print("--- BOUNDS, ANTIMERIDIAN-AWARE ---")
    Assert(Not BoxWraps(GeoRouteBounds(Route())), "A EUROPEAN ROUTE NEEDS NO WRAPPING")
    Assert(BoxWraps(GeoRouteBounds(LineRoute())), "AND ONE ACROSS THE LINE REPORTS THAT IT DOES")
    Assert(Close(BoxWest(GeoRouteBounds(LineRoute())), 179, 0.000001), "THE BOX RUNS EAST FROM 179 EAST")
    Assert(Close(BoxEast(GeoRouteBounds(LineRoute())), -179, 0.000001), "TO 179 WEST, WHICH IS TWO DEGREES AND NOT THREE HUNDRED AND FIFTY-EIGHT")
    Assert(GeoInBox(EastOfLine(), GeoRouteBounds(LineRoute())), "AND GEOINBOX AGREES ABOUT ITS OWN POINTS")
    Assert(GeoInBox(WestOfLine(), GeoRouteBounds(LineRoute())), "AT BOTH ENDS")
    Assert(Not GeoInBox(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoRouteBounds(LineRoute())), "AND EXCLUDES THE FAR SIDE OF THE PLANET")
    Assert(GeoInBox(London(), GeoRouteBounds(Route())), "AN ORDINARY BOX CONTAINS ITS OWN POINTS TOO")
    Assert(Not GeoInBox(NewYork(), GeoRouteBounds(Route())), "AND NOT SOMEWHERE ELSE")

    Print("--- A BOX AROUND A RADIUS, FOR CHEAP FILTERING ---")
    Assert(GeoInBox(London(), GeoBoxAround(London(), 1000)), "A BOX AROUND A POINT CONTAINS IT")
    Assert(GeoInBox(GeoDestination(London(), 0, 900), GeoBoxAround(London(), 1000)), "AND A POINT 900 M NORTH OF IT")
    Assert(Not GeoInBox(GeoDestination(London(), 0, 2000), GeoBoxAround(London(), 1000)), "AND NOT ONE 2 KM NORTH")
    Assert(Close(BoxWest(GeoBoxAround(GeoAt(89.9, 0), 100000)), -180, 0.000001), "NEAR A POLE IT WIDENS TO EVERY LONGITUDE, WHICH IS CORRECT AND SURPRISING")
    Assert(Close(BoxNorth(GeoBoxAround(GeoAt(89.9, 0), 100000)), 90, 0.000001), "AND CLAMPS LATITUDE AT THE POLE")

    Print("--- UNION AND CENTRE ---")
    Assert(GeoInBox(GeoAt(0, 179.5), GeoBoxUnion(GeoBoxAround(GeoAt(0, 179.5), 10000), GeoBoxAround(GeoAt(0, -179.5), 10000))), "THE UNION CONTAINS THE FIRST BOX")
    Assert(GeoInBox(GeoAt(0, -179.5), GeoBoxUnion(GeoBoxAround(GeoAt(0, 179.5), 10000), GeoBoxAround(GeoAt(0, -179.5), 10000))), "AND THE SECOND")
    Assert(Not GeoInBox(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoBoxUnion(GeoBoxAround(GeoAt(0, 179.5), 10000), GeoBoxAround(GeoAt(0, -179.5), 10000))), "AND DOES NOT SWALLOW THE PLANET TO GET THEM")
    Assert(Close(Abs(GeoLon(GeoBoxCentre(GeoRouteBounds(LineRoute())))), 180, 0.000001), "THE CENTRE OF A WRAPPING BOX IS ON THE LINE, NOT AT ZERO")

    Print("--- THE ENCLOSING CIRCLE ---")
    Assert(GeoDistance(CircleCentre(GeoBoundingCircle(Route())), London()) <= CircleRadius(GeoBoundingCircle(Route())) + 0.001, "THE CIRCLE COVERS THE FIRST POINT")
    Assert(GeoDistance(CircleCentre(GeoBoundingCircle(Route())), Nth(Route(), 3)) <= CircleRadius(GeoBoundingCircle(Route())) + 0.001, "AND THE LAST")

    Print("--- SIMPLIFY ---")
    Assert(Length(GeoSimplify({ GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 5), GeoAt(0, 10) }, 1)) = 2, "A POINT ON THE LINE IS NOISE, AND GOES")
    Assert(Length(GeoSimplify({ GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(1, 5), GeoAt(0, 10) }, 1)) = 3, "AND A REAL CORNER STAYS")
    Assert(GeoNear(First(GeoSimplify(Route(), 1000)), London(), 0.000001), "SIMPLIFY PRESERVES THE FIRST POINT")
    Assert(GeoNear(Nth(GeoSimplify(Route(), 1000), Length(GeoSimplify(Route(), 1000))), Nth(Route(), 3), 0.000001), "AND THE LAST")
    Assert(Length(GeoSimplify(Route(), 1000)) <= Length(Route()), "AND NEVER GROWS A ROUTE")

    Print("--- RESAMPLE ---")
    Assert(Length(GeoResample({ GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 1) }, 1000000)) = 2, "A SPACING LONGER THAN THE ROUTE ANSWERS TWO POINTS")
    Assert(GeoNear(First(GeoResample(Route(), 50000)), London(), 0.000001), "RESAMPLE KEEPS THE FIRST POINT")
    Assert(GeoNear(Nth(GeoResample(Route(), 50000), Length(GeoResample(Route(), 50000))), Nth(Route(), 3), 0.000001), "AND THE LAST")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(First(GeoResample(Route(), 50000)), Nth(GeoResample(Route(), 50000), 2)), 50000, 0.001), "AND THE SPACING IS THE SPACING ASKED FOR")

    Print("--- WAYPOINTS, THE DRAWING WORD ---")
    Assert(Length(GeoWaypoints(London(), NewYork(), 5)) = 5, "FIVE WAYPOINTS ARE FIVE POINTS")
    Assert(GeoNear(First(GeoWaypoints(London(), NewYork(), 5)), London(), 0.001), "THE FIRST IS THE START")
    Assert(GeoNear(Nth(GeoWaypoints(London(), NewYork(), 5), 5), NewYork(), 0.001), "AND THE LAST IS THE END")
    Assert(GeoNear(Nth(GeoWaypoints(London(), NewYork(), 5), 3), GeoMidpoint(London(), NewYork()), 0.001), "AND THE MIDDLE ONE IS THE MIDPOINT, WHICH IS WHY THE DRAWN LINE CURVES")

    Print("--- CENTROID, THROUGH 3-D VECTORS ---")
    Assert(Close(Abs(GeoLon(GeoCentroid(LineRoute()))), 180, 0.000001), "THE CENTROID ACROSS THE LINE IS ON THE LINE, NOT IN THE GULF OF GUINEA")
    Assert(Close(GeoLat(GeoCentroid(LineRoute())), 0, 0.000001), "AND STAYS ON THE EQUATOR")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoCentroid({ London() }), London(), 0.000001), "THE CENTROID OF ONE POINT IS THAT POINT")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoCentroid({ London(), London() }), London(), 0.000001), "AND OF THE SAME POINT TWICE")

    Print("--- AREA, BY SPHERICAL EXCESS ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoArea({ GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 10), GeoAt(10, 0) }), 621357420100, 1000000), "A TEN-DEGREE TRIANGLE, AGAINST THE EXCESS WORKED INDEPENDENTLY")
    Assert(Close(GeoArea({ GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 90), GeoAt(90, 0) }), Pi() * GeoRadius() ^ 2 / 2, 1000), "AND AN OCTANT OF THE SPHERE IS AN EIGHTH OF ITS SURFACE")
    Assert(Close(GeoArea({ GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 10), GeoAt(10, 0), GeoAt(0, 0) }), GeoArea({ GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 10), GeoAt(10, 0) }), 0.000001), "A RING THE CALLER CLOSED AND ONE IT DID NOT ARE THE SAME RING")
    Rem One square metre out of six hundred and twenty-one square
    Rem kilometres. The tolerance is a square metre and not the
    Rem micrometre used elsewhere in this file because the two windings
    Rem do not take the same arithmetic path: one walks the ring, the
    Rem other walks it reversed, and the vertex angles are summed in the
    Rem opposite order. Asking for closer than this would be asking a
    Rem double for nineteen significant digits.
    Assert(Close(GeoArea({ GeoAt(10, 0), GeoAt(0, 10), GeoAt(0, 0) }), GeoArea({ GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 10), GeoAt(10, 0) }), 1), "AND WINDING THE OTHER WAY DOES NOT CHANGE IT")

    Print("--- DEGREES, MINUTES AND SECONDS ---")
    Assert(GeoDms(53.72, 1) = "53" & DegMark() & "43'12.0" & SecMark(), "53.72 DEGREES WRITTEN OUT")
    Assert(GeoDms(-1.86, 1) = "-1" & DegMark() & "51'36.0" & SecMark(), "AND A WESTERN LONGITUDE KEEPS ITS SIGN ON THE DEGREES")
    Assert(GeoDms(5.5, 0) = "5" & DegMark() & "30'00" & SecMark(), "MINUTES AND SECONDS ARE ZERO-PADDED TO TWO DIGITS")

    Print("--- READING DMS BACK ---")
    Assert(Close(OkNum(GeoFromDms("53" & DegMark() & "43'12.0" & SecMark()), 0), 53.72, 0.0000001), "THE ROUND TRIP, NORTH")
    Assert(Close(OkNum(GeoFromDms("-1 51 36"), 0), -1.86, 0.0000001), "PLAIN ASCII, AND THE SIGN ON THE DEGREES")
    Assert(Close(OkNum(GeoFromDms("1 51 36 W"), 0), -1.86, 0.0000001), "A HEMISPHERE LETTER AFTER")
    Assert(Close(OkNum(GeoFromDms("W1 51 36"), 0), -1.86, 0.0000001), "AND ONE BEFORE")
    Assert(Close(OkNum(GeoFromDms(GeoDms(-33.8688, 4)), 0), -33.8688, 0.0001), "SOUTHERN LATITUDES ROUND-TRIP TOO")
    Assert(Close(OkNum(GeoFromDms(GeoDms(174.7762, 4)), 0), 174.7762, 0.0001), "AND EASTERN LONGITUDES")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoFromDms("53 43 12 X")), "A CHARACTER IT CANNOT READ IS AN ERR")
    Assert(ErrAt(GeoFromDms("53 43 12 X")) = 10, "AND THE ERR CARRIES ITS 1-BASED POSITION")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoFromDms("1.2.3")), "AND SO IS SOMETHING THAT ONLY LOOKS LIKE A NUMBER")

    Print("--- THE PASTE FORM EVERY MAPPING TOOL ACCEPTS ---")
    Assert(GeoFormat(GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 6) = "53.720000, -1.860000", "LATITUDE, COMMA, LONGITUDE")

    Print("--- PARSING A WHOLE COORDINATE, IN EVERY SPELLING ---")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoParse("53.72, -1.86")), GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 0.001), "A DECIMAL PAIR")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoParse("53.72 -1.86")), GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 0.001), "WITH NO COMMA")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoParse("53 43 12 N, 1 51 36 W")), GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 0.001), "DMS WITH THE LETTERS AFTER")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoParse("N53 43 12 W1 51 36")), GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 0.001), "DMS WITH THE LETTERS BEFORE")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoParse("53" & DegMark() & "43'12" & SecMark() & "N 1" & DegMark() & "51'36" & SecMark() & "W")), GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 0.001), "DMS WITH THE MARKS")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoParse("1 51 36 W, 53 43 12 N")), GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 0.001), "LONGITUDE FIRST, BECAUSE THE LETTERS SAY WHICH IS WHICH")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoParse("53 43 -1 51")), GeoAt(53 + 43 / 60, Negate(1 + 51 / 60)), 0.001), "FOUR BARE NUMBERS SPLIT EVENLY")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoParse(GeoFormat(NewYork(), 6))), NewYork(), 0.5), "AND GEOFORMAT ROUND-TRIPS THROUGH IT")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoParse("53.72, -1.86, 99")), "THREE COORDINATES ARE NOT A COORDINATE")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoParse("91, 0")), "AND A LATITUDE OUT OF DOMAIN IS REFUSED HERE TOO")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoParse("")), "AND SO IS NOTHING AT ALL")
    Assert(ErrAt(GeoParse("53.72, -1.86Q")) = 13, "AN UNREADABLE CHARACTER IS NAMED BY POSITION")

    Print("--- SIXTEEN COMPASS POINTS, NOT THIRTY-TWO ---")
    Assert(GeoCompass(0) = "N", "NORTH")
    Assert(GeoCompass(22.5) = "NNE", "NORTH NORTH EAST")
    Assert(GeoCompass(45) = "NE", "NORTH EAST")
    Assert(GeoCompass(180) = "S", "SOUTH")
    Assert(GeoCompass(350) = "N", "AND THE LAST SECTOR WRAPS BACK TO NORTH")
    Assert(GeoCompass(11.24) = "N", "THE SECTOR BOUNDARY IS AT 11.25")
    Assert(GeoCompass(11.26) = "NNE", "ON BOTH SIDES OF IT")
    Assert(Close(OkNum(GeoFromCompass("NNE"), 0), 22.5, 0.000001), "AND BACK AGAIN")
    Assert(Close(OkNum(GeoFromCompass("wsw"), 0), 247.5, 0.000001), "CASE DOES NOT MATTER")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoFromCompass("NEbN")), "A THIRTY-TWO POINT HALF-WIND IS NOT A WORD THIS MACHINE KNOWS")

    Print("--- GEOHASH: THE FIRST CHARACTER, WORKED BY HAND ---")
    Assert(Left(GeoHash(GeoAt(51.5, -0.1), 5), 1) = "g", "LONDON IS IN CELL 01111, WHICH IS G")
    Assert(Left(GeoHash(NewYork(), 5), 1) = "d", "NEW YORK IS IN 01100, WHICH IS D")
    Assert(Left(GeoHash(GeoAt(-33.8688, 151.2093), 5), 1) = "r", "AND SYDNEY IS IN 10111, WHICH IS R")
    Assert(Len(GeoHash(London(), 9)) = 9, "NINE CHARACTERS ARE ASKED FOR AND NINE ARRIVE")

    Print("--- A GEOHASH IS A BOX, NOT A POINT ---")
    Assert(Close(BoxEast(OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))) - BoxWest(OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))), 360 / 2 ^ 15, 0.0000001), "A SIX-CHARACTER CELL IS 15 LONGITUDE BITS WIDE")
    Assert(Close(BoxNorth(OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))) - BoxSouth(OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))), 180 / 2 ^ 15, 0.0000001), "AND 15 LATITUDE BITS TALL")
    Assert(BoxEast(OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))) - BoxWest(OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))) > BoxNorth(OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))) - BoxSouth(OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))), "WIDER THAN IT IS TALL, WHICH IS WHAT CATCHES AN INTERLEAVE PUT IN BACKWARDS")
    Assert(GeoInBox(London(), OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))), "THE CELL CONTAINS THE POINT THAT MADE IT")
    Assert(GeoInBox(OkPt(GeoFromHash(GeoHash(London(), 6))), OkBox(GeoHashBox(GeoHash(London(), 6)))), "AND THE CENTRE GEOFROMHASH ANSWERS IS INSIDE IT")

    Print("--- GEOHASH ROUND TRIPS, ALL FOUR QUADRANTS ---")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoFromHash(GeoHash(GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 9))), GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 5), "NORTH WEST, TO THE CELL AND NOT TO THE POINT")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoFromHash(GeoHash(GeoAt(35.68, 139.77), 9))), GeoAt(35.68, 139.77), 5), "NORTH EAST")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoFromHash(GeoHash(GeoAt(-33.87, 151.21), 9))), GeoAt(-33.87, 151.21), 5), "SOUTH EAST")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoFromHash(GeoHash(GeoAt(-34.6, -58.38), 9))), GeoAt(-34.6, -58.38), 5), "AND SOUTH WEST")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoHashBox("abc")), "A IS NOT IN THE GEOHASH ALPHABET - IT DROPS A, I, L AND O")
    Assert(ErrAt(GeoHashBox("gcpua")) = 5, "AND THE ERR NAMES THE OFFENDING POSITION")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoHashBox("")), "NOR IS NOTHING A GEOHASH")

    Print("--- THE EIGHT NEIGHBOURS, WHICH ARE WHAT MAKE IT USEFUL ---")
    Assert(Length(GeoHashNeighbours(GeoHash(London(), 6))) = 8, "EIGHT OF THEM")
    Assert(Not HasText(GeoHashNeighbours(GeoHash(London(), 6)), GeoHash(London(), 6)), "AND NONE OF THEM IS THE CELL ITSELF")
    Assert(AllDistinct(GeoHashNeighbours(GeoHash(London(), 6))), "AND NO TWO OF THEM ARE THE SAME CELL")

    Print("--- MAIDENHEAD, BECAUSE IT IS REAL AND DELIGHTFUL ---")
    Assert(GeoLocator(GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 6) = "IO93br", "THE HEAVY WOOLLEN DISTRICT, WORKED BY HAND")
    Assert(GeoLocator(GeoAt(51.5074, -0.1278), 6) = "IO91wm", "AND LONDON")
    Assert(GeoLocator(GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 4) = "IO93", "FOUR CHARACTERS IS THE SQUARE")
    Assert(GeoLocator(GeoAt(53.72, -1.86), 2) = "IO", "AND TWO IS THE FIELD")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoFromLocator("IO91wm")), GeoAt(51.5074, -0.1278), 4000), "READING ONE BACK LANDS IN THE SAME SUBSQUARE")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoFromLocator(GeoLocator(GeoAt(-33.87, 151.21), 8))), GeoAt(-33.87, 151.21), 500), "AN EIGHT-CHARACTER LOCATOR ROUND-TRIPS IN THE SOUTHERN HEMISPHERE")
    Assert(GeoNear(OkPt(GeoFromLocator(GeoLocator(GeoAt(-34.6, -58.38), 8))), GeoAt(-34.6, -58.38), 500), "AND IN THE SOUTH WEST")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoFromLocator("IO9")), "AN ODD NUMBER OF CHARACTERS IS NOT A LOCATOR")
    Assert(IsErr(GeoFromLocator("ZZ93br")), "AND Z IS PAST THE END OF THE FIELD ALPHABET")

    Print("--- THE JULIAN DAY, WORKED BY HAND ---")
    Assert(GeoJulian(2000, 1, 1) = 2451544.5, "THE FIRST OF JANUARY 2000 AT MIDNIGHT UT")
    Assert(GeoJulian(2024, 3, 21) - GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20) = 1, "CONSECUTIVE DAYS ARE ONE APART")
    Assert(GeoJulian(2025, 1, 1) - GeoJulian(2024, 1, 1) = 366, "2024 WAS A LEAP YEAR")
    Assert(GeoJulian(1900, 3, 1) - GeoJulian(1900, 2, 28) = 1, "AND 1900 WAS NOT, WHICH IS THE CENTURY RULE")

    Print("--- THE SEASON, AS ONE NUMBER ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoSolarDeclination(GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 23.44, 0.06), "THE JUNE SOLSTICE IS THE OBLIQUITY OF THE ECLIPTIC")
    Assert(Close(GeoSolarDeclination(GeoJulian(2024, 12, 21)), -23.44, 0.06), "AND THE DECEMBER ONE IS ITS NEGATIVE")
    Assert(Close(GeoSolarDeclination(GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20)), 0, 0.5), "AT THE MARCH EQUINOX THE SUN IS OVER THE EQUATOR")
    Assert(Close(GeoSolarDeclination(GeoJulian(2024, 9, 22)), 0, 0.5), "AND AT THE SEPTEMBER ONE TOO")

    Print("--- WHY A SUNDIAL DISAGREES WITH A CLOCK ---")
    Assert(Abs(GeoEquationOfTime(GeoJulian(2024, 2, 11))) < 17, "THE EQUATION OF TIME NEVER EXCEEDS SEVENTEEN MINUTES")
    Assert(Abs(GeoEquationOfTime(GeoJulian(2024, 11, 3))) < 17, "AT EITHER EXTREME")
    Assert(GeoEquationOfTime(GeoJulian(2024, 2, 11)) < 0, "IN FEBRUARY THE SUNDIAL IS BEHIND THE CLOCK")
    Assert(GeoEquationOfTime(GeoJulian(2024, 11, 3)) > 0, "AND IN NOVEMBER IT IS AHEAD")

    Print("--- SOLAR NOON ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoSunNoon(GeoAt(51.5, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 12, 0.3), "ON THE PRIME MERIDIAN NOON IS NEAR TWELVE, OFF BY THE EQUATION OF TIME")
    Assert(Close(GeoSunNoon(GeoAt(0, 15), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)) + 1, GeoSunNoon(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 0.000001), "AND FIFTEEN DEGREES EAST IS AN HOUR EARLIER")

    Print("--- THE SUN IS WHERE THE RISE SAYS IT IS ---")
    Rem The definitive self-consistency check of this whole part: ask
    Rem GeoSunRise for a time, then ask GeoSunPos where the sun is AT
    Rem that time. It has to be at the sunrise altitude, or one of the
    Rem two words is wrong. It ties the position model, the equation of
    Rem time, the declination and solar noon together in one assertion.
    Assert(Close(SunElevation(GeoSunPos(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20), SomeNum(GeoSunRise(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 0))), GeoSunAltitude(), 0.15), "LONDON, MIDSUMMER")
    Assert(Close(SunElevation(GeoSunPos(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 12, 21), SomeNum(GeoSunSet(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 12, 21)), 0))), GeoSunAltitude(), 0.15), "LONDON, MIDWINTER SUNSET")
    Assert(Close(SunElevation(GeoSunPos(GeoAt(-33.8688, 151.2093), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20), SomeNum(GeoSunRise(GeoAt(-33.8688, 151.2093), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 0))), GeoSunAltitude(), 0.15), "SYDNEY, SOUTHERN HEMISPHERE")
    Assert(Close(SunElevation(GeoSunPos(GeoAt(-0.1807, -78.4678), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20), SomeNum(GeoSunRise(GeoAt(-0.1807, -78.4678), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20)), 0))), GeoSunAltitude(), 0.15), "QUITO, ON THE EQUATOR")

    Print("--- NOON ELEVATION IS 90 LESS THE ZENITH DISTANCE ---")
    Assert(Close(SunElevation(GeoSunPos(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20), GeoSunNoon(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)))), 90 - Abs(GeoLat(London()) - GeoSolarDeclination(GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20))), 0.1), "LONDON AT MIDSUMMER NOON")
    Assert(Close(SunElevation(GeoSunPos(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20), GeoSunNoon(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20)))), 90 - Abs(0 - GeoSolarDeclination(GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20))), 0.1), "AND THE EQUATOR AT AN EQUINOX, WHERE IT IS OVERHEAD")
    Assert(CloseAngle(SunAzimuth(GeoSunPos(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20), GeoSunNoon(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)))), 180, 0.5), "AT NOON IN THE NORTH THE SUN IS DUE SOUTH")
    Assert(CloseAngle(SunAzimuth(GeoSunPos(GeoAt(-33.8688, 151.2093), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20), GeoSunNoon(GeoAt(-33.8688, 151.2093), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)))), 0, 0.5), "AND IN THE SOUTH IT IS DUE NORTH")

    Print("--- RISE AND SET STRADDLE NOON ---")
    Assert(Close(SomeNum(GeoSunRise(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 0) + SomeNum(GeoSunSet(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 0), 2 * GeoSunNoon(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 0.000001), "THEY ARE SYMMETRIC ABOUT SOLAR NOON, BY CONSTRUCTION")
    Assert(SomeNum(GeoSunRise(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 0) < SomeNum(GeoSunSet(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 0), "AND THE SUN RISES BEFORE IT SETS")

    Print("--- DAY LENGTH ---")
    Assert(Close(GeoDayLength(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20)), 12.11, 0.05), "TWELVE HOURS ON THE EQUATOR, PLUS THE REFRACTION AT BOTH ENDS")
    Assert(Close(GeoDayLength(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 12.11, 0.05), "AND THE EQUATOR HARDLY VARIES ACROSS THE YEAR")
    Assert(Close(GeoDayLength(GeoAt(40, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20)), GeoDayLength(GeoAt(-40, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20)), 0.05), "AT AN EQUINOX BOTH HEMISPHERES GET THE SAME DAY")
    Assert(GeoDayLength(GeoAt(60, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)) > 18, "SIXTY NORTH GETS OVER EIGHTEEN HOURS AT MIDSUMMER")
    Assert(GeoDayLength(GeoAt(-60, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)) < 6, "AND SIXTY SOUTH GETS UNDER SIX ON THE SAME DAY")
    Assert(Close(GeoDayLength(GeoAt(70, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 24, 0.000001), "INSIDE THE ARCTIC CIRCLE IN JUNE THE SUN NEVER SETS")
    Assert(Close(GeoDayLength(GeoAt(70, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 12, 21)), 0, 0.000001), "AND IN DECEMBER IT NEVER RISES")

    Print("--- OPTION IS THE WHOLE DESIGN HERE ---")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoSunRise(GeoAt(70, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20))), "NO SUNRISE ABOVE THE ARCTIC CIRCLE IN JUNE, BECAUSE IT NEVER SET")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoSunSet(GeoAt(70, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20))), "AND NO SUNSET, FOR THE SAME REASON")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoSunRise(GeoAt(70, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 12, 21))), "AND NONE IN DECEMBER EITHER, FOR THE OPPOSITE REASON")
    Assert(Not IsNone(GeoSunRise(GeoAt(70, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20))), "BUT AT THE EQUINOX IT RISES THERE LIKE ANYWHERE ELSE")
    Assert(Close(GeoSunNoon(GeoAt(70, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20)), 12, 0.3), "SOLAR NOON IS DEFINED EVEN WHERE RISE AND SET ARE NOT, WHICH IS WHY IT IS SEPARATE")

    Print("--- TWILIGHT ---")
    Assert(Length(SomeNums(GeoTwilight(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20), 6))) = 2, "CIVIL TWILIGHT IS A PAIR OF TIMES")
    Assert(First(SomeNums(GeoTwilight(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20), 6))) < SomeNum(GeoSunRise(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20)), 0), "THE MORNING ONE COMES BEFORE SUNRISE")
    Assert(Nth(SomeNums(GeoTwilight(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20), 6)), 2) > SomeNum(GeoSunSet(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20)), 0), "AND THE EVENING ONE AFTER SUNSET")
    Assert(First(SomeNums(GeoTwilight(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20), 18))) < First(SomeNums(GeoTwilight(London(), GeoJulian(2024, 3, 20), 6))), "ASTRONOMICAL TWILIGHT STARTS BEFORE CIVIL")
    Assert(IsNone(GeoTwilight(GeoAt(70, 0), GeoJulian(2024, 6, 20), 18)), "AND THERE IS NO ASTRONOMICAL TWILIGHT UNDER THE MIDNIGHT SUN")

    Print("--- A RHUMB LINE IS NOT A GREAT CIRCLE, AND THAT IS THE POINT ---")
    Assert(GeoRhumbDistance(London(), NewYork()) > GeoDistance(London(), NewYork()), "THE CONSTANT-BEARING TRACK IS THE LONGER ONE")
    Assert(GeoRhumbDistance(London(), NewYork()) - GeoDistance(London(), NewYork()) > 50000, "AND ACROSS THE ATLANTIC IT IS LONGER BY OVER FIFTY KILOMETRES")
    Assert(Close(GeoRhumbDistance(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(50, 0)), GeoDistance(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(50, 0)), 0.001), "ALONG A MERIDIAN THE TWO AGREE, BECAUSE A MERIDIAN IS BOTH")
    Assert(Close(GeoRhumbDistance(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 50)), GeoDistance(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(0, 50)), 0.001), "AND ALONG THE EQUATOR TOO")
    Assert(Close(GeoRhumbBearing(GeoAt(0, 0), GeoAt(50, 0)), 0, 0.000001), "DUE NORTH IS DUE NORTH")
    Rem The same two points, both ways round, at a latitude where the
    Rem difference is unmistakable. Fifty north rather than ten north
    Rem because the great circle's deviation grows with the latitude:
    Rem down at ten it is under five degrees, which would make this a
    Rem test that only just passes rather than one that shows the point.
    Assert(CloseAngle(GeoRhumbBearing(GeoAt(50, 0), GeoAt(50, 50)), 90, 0.000001), "A PARALLEL IS DUE EAST ALL THE WAY BY RHUMB")
    Assert(Abs(GeoBearing(GeoAt(50, 0), GeoAt(50, 50)) - 90) > 15, "AND THE GREAT CIRCLE BETWEEN THE SAME TWO POINTS LEAVES MORE THAN FIFTEEN DEGREES NORTH OF EAST")

    Print("--- THE BEARING YOU ACTUALLY STEER STAYS PUT ---")
    Assert(CloseAngle(GeoRhumbBearing(London(), GeoRhumbDestination(London(), 231, 3000000)), 231, 0.0001), "STEER 231 FOR 3000 KM AND THE RHUMB BEARING BACK IS STILL 231")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoRhumbDestination(London(), GeoRhumbBearing(London(), NewYork()), GeoRhumbDistance(London(), NewYork())), NewYork(), 1), "AND THE RHUMB ROUND TRIP CLOSES WITHIN A METRE")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoRhumbDestination(GeoAt(0, 179), 90, 222390), GeoAt(0, -179), 1), "A RHUMB LEG ACROSS THE ANTIMERIDIAN ARRIVES ON THE OTHER SIDE")
    Assert(Close(GeoRhumbDistance(GeoAt(0, 179), GeoAt(0, -179)), 222390.1605, 1), "AND MEASURES THE SHORT WAY ROUND")

    Print("--- HOW FAR YOU CAN SEE ---")
    Assert(GeoHorizon(0) = 0, "FROM SEA LEVEL YOU SEE NOTHING PAST YOUR FEET")
    Assert(Close(GeoHorizon(2), Sqr(2 * GeoRadius() * 2), 0.01), "AND FROM EYE HEIGHT THE SMALL-ANGLE IDENTITY HOLDS")
    Assert(Close(GeoHorizon(2), 5048.2, 1), "WHICH IS THE FAMILIAR FIVE KILOMETRES")
    Assert(GeoHorizon(100) > GeoHorizon(10), "HIGHER IS FURTHER")
    Assert(Close(GeoGeographicRange(30, 5), GeoHorizon(30) + GeoHorizon(5), 0.000001), "AND A LIGHT COMES INTO VIEW WHERE THE TWO HORIZONS MEET")

    Print("--- DEAD RECKONING, WHICH IS FOLD IN ONE WORD ---")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoDeadReckon(London(), { { 90, 1000 } }), GeoDestination(London(), 90, 1000), 0.000001), "ONE LEG IS ONE DESTINATION")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoDeadReckon(London(), { }), London(), 0.000001), "AND NO LEGS AT ALL LEAVES YOU WHERE YOU STARTED")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoDeadReckon(GeoAt(10, 20), { { 0, 500000 }, { 180, 500000 } }), GeoAt(10, 20), 0.001), "NORTH THEN SOUTH THE SAME DISTANCE COMES HOME")
    Assert(Close(GeoDistance(London(), GeoDeadReckon(London(), { { 45, 100000 }, { 45, 100000 } })), GeoDistance(London(), GeoDestination(London(), 45, 200000)), 5000), "AND TWO LEGS ON ONE BEARING ARE ABOUT ONE LONG ONE - ABOUT, BECAUSE A GREAT CIRCLE TURNS UNDER YOU")

    Print("--- THE NAUTICAL TIME ZONE, WHICH IS ARITHMETIC ---")
    Assert(GeoZoneOffset(0) = 0, "GREENWICH IS ZONE ZERO")
    Assert(GeoZoneOffset(7.4) = 0, "AND SO IS ANYWHERE INSIDE ITS SEVEN AND A HALF DEGREES")
    Assert(GeoZoneOffset(7.6) = 1, "JUST PAST THE EDGE IS THE NEXT ZONE")
    Assert(GeoZoneOffset(-75) = -5, "SEVENTY-FIVE WEST IS FIVE HOURS BEHIND")
    Assert(GeoZoneOffset(175) = 12, "AND THE FAR SIDE IS TWELVE AHEAD")

    Print("--- EARTH-CENTRED CARTESIAN, THE BRIDGE TO THREE DIMENSIONS ---")
    Assert(Close(Nth(GeoEcef(GeoAt(0, 0), 0), 1), GeoRadius(), 0.000001), "X RUNS OUT THROUGH ZERO NORTH ZERO EAST")
    Assert(Close(Nth(GeoEcef(GeoAt(0, 90), 0), 2), GeoRadius(), 0.000001), "Y THROUGH THE EQUATOR AT NINETY EAST")
    Assert(Close(Nth(GeoEcef(GeoAt(90, 0), 0), 3), GeoRadius(), 0.000001), "AND Z THROUGH THE NORTH POLE")
    Assert(Close(GeoEcefHeight(GeoEcef(London(), 8000)), 8000, 0.000001), "THE ALTITUDE SURVIVES THE TRIP OUT AND BACK")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoFromEcef(GeoEcef(London(), 8000)), London(), 0.000001), "AND SO DOES THE POSITION, WITH THE HEIGHT DISCARDED")
    Assert(GeoNear(GeoFromEcef(GeoEcef(GeoAt(-34.6, -58.38), 0)), GeoAt(-34.6, -58.38), 0.000001), "IN THE SOUTHERN AND WESTERN HEMISPHERES TOO")

    Print("ALL ASSERTIONS PASSED")
